  79:     - Colored components outside the frame touching its edges.
  80: 
  81:     Rule:
  82:     - Output = the frame's interior, filled with the fill color.
  83:     - Map each outside component's frame-touch points into interior coordinates.
  84:     - Monochrome components become solid Manhattan stripes between mapped endpoints.
  85:     - Two-color components become alternating-color Manhattan paths.
  86: 
  87:     Key insight: Endpoint colors of two-color traces anchor the alternating phase deterministically.
